# Explore Banks tooltips

When researching or writing field/column help on Explore Banks:

1. Read and follow `.cursor/skills/shroffin-explore-tooltips/SKILL.md`.
2. **Research** new fields → `.cursor/skills/shroffin-explore-tooltips/research.md` (same method as the original briefs).
3. **Write** tips → `.cursor/skills/shroffin-explore-tooltips/craft.md` + `super-review-1/explore-banks/_tooltip-research-briefs.md`.
4. Locked lines (if revising): `super-review-1/explore-banks/_tooltip-approved-copy.md`.

Do not invent a new research style or tip style. Do not lightly polish old live tips. If a field has no research brief yet, research it before writing the tip.

**Hard ban — capacity metaphors:** never write “EMI room”, “share that room”, “room for”, “FOIR room”, “eat the same pie”, or soft “headroom” for FOIR in tips. Say the plain consequence (e.g. existing EMIs reduce what lenders allow for a new home EMI).
